Well, you were saying you wanted to work on it; I was just trying to better understand the scenario where it comes up before making a decision like that.
Well I think this can be useful when the user is making inputs there as recorded as tuple and after this rendered down like a map for example.
@masenf what is your opinion
Looking through the code, it seems we're already very close to supporting this:

https://github.com/reflex-dev/reflex/blob/76b8af3b42a618939c1fd7dd8af5dfaad9f5906b/reflex/app.py#L329-L330

We already wrap the returned component in an `rx.Fragment`, so it seems like this bit of code could attempt to splat the component into the fragment and if that gets a `TypeError` (not iterable), then just pass the component normally.

Maybe something like

```python
try:
    component = Fragment.create(*component)
except TypeError:
    component = Fragment.create(component)
```

I think it would work and the change doesn't seem too invasive, but we'll need tests and doc updates to go along with it.
