problem_statement:
dynamic icons causes next to never halt
![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/74d61a44-970a-40ae-89cc-cd6d380719ce)

When using rx.match for example in gathering icon by dict/list using a foreach it rises the cpu to 50+%

When removing the rx component addition it "only" adds 20% on each tab

code example:

```python
import reflex as rx

class LandingState(rx.State):
    features: dict[str, dict] = {
        "fast": {
            "title": "test1",
            "description": "test2",
            "icon": "zap"
        },
        "secure": {
            "title": "test2",
            "description": "test2",
            "icon": "lock"
        },
        "global": {
            "title": "test3",
            "description": "test3",
            "icon": "globe"
        }
    }

def feature_card(feature: str) -> rx.Component:

    icon_name = rx.match(
        feature,
        ("fast", "zap"),
        ("secure", "lock"),
        ("global", "globe"),
        "zap"  # Default fallback
    )

    return rx.card(
        rx.vstack(
            rx.icon(
                icon_name,
                size=32,
            ),
        ),
    )

def features_section() -> rx.Component:
    return rx.vstack(
        rx.hstack(
            rx.foreach(
                LandingState.features.keys(),
                lambda feature: feature_card(feature)
            ),
            spacing="6",
            justify="center",
            wrap="wrap",
            width="100%",
            padding="2em",
        ),
    )

@rx.page(route="/test", title="Test")
def test() -> rx.Component:
    return rx.vstack(
        features_section(),
        spacing="0",
        width="100%",
        background="#151515",
    )
```

CSS in a file name called "styles.css" doesn't get loaded
**Describe the bug**

